User tested WhatsApp interactive messages (buttons/lists) successfully. Both message types return structured webhook responses with IDs for flow execution. Phase 1 validated, Phase 2 implements full data layer.

## Phase 1: POC Validation ✅

- Documented successful tests of interactive buttons and lists to phone 555499250023
- Confirmed webhook payloads contain `button_reply.id` and `list_reply.id` for flow matching
- Updated `POC_RESULTS.md` with actual webhook responses

## Phase 2: Data Infrastructure ✅

### Database (`supabase/migrations/20251206_create_interactive_flows.sql`)

Two tables with full multi-tenant isolation:

```sql
-- Flow definitions
interactive_flows (
  id, client_id, name, trigger_type, trigger_keywords,
  blocks JSONB,  -- Array of FlowBlock
  edges JSONB,   -- Array of FlowEdge
  start_block_id, is_active, ...
)

-- Runtime execution state
flow_executions (
  id, flow_id, client_id, phone,
  current_block_id, variables JSONB, history JSONB,
  status, ...
)
```

- 8 indexes including GIN on keywords, composite on (client_id, phone, status)
- RLS policies enforce client_id ownership on all operations
- Unique constraint: one active execution per contact

### Types (`src/types/interactiveFlows.ts`)

Complete type system with 11 block types (start, message, interactive_list, interactive_buttons, condition, action, ai_handoff, human_handoff, delay, webhook, end):

```typescript
export interface InteractiveFlow {
  id: string;
  clientId: string;
  triggerType: 'keyword' | 'qr_code' | 'link' | 'manual' | 'always';
  triggerKeywords?: string[];
  blocks: FlowBlock[];
  edges: FlowEdge[];
  startBlockId: string;
}

export interface FlowExecution {
  id: string;
  flowId: string;
  phone: string;
  currentBlockId: string;
  variables: Record<string, any>;
  history: FlowStep[];
  status: 'active' | 'completed' | 'transferred_ai' | 'transferred_human';
}
```

Constants: `INTERACTIVE_MESSAGE_LIMITS` (WhatsApp API limits), `FLOW_DEFAULTS`

### CRUD APIs

Standard pattern: auth check → fetch client_id from user_profiles → enforce RLS via client_id → transform DB format to API format

- `GET /api/flows` - List with filters (active, triggerType) and pagination
- `POST /api/flows` - Create with validation (name, triggerType, blocks, startBlockId)
- `GET /api/flows/[flowId]` - Fetch single flow
- `PUT /api/flows/[flowId]` - Partial update with block validation
- `DELETE /api/flows/[flowId]` - Cascade to flow_executions

All endpoints return proper status codes (400/401/403/404/500) with error messages.

## Migration Required

User must run: `supabase db push`

## Progress

21/52 tasks complete (40%). Next: Phase 3 Flow Executor.

