Game thread was consuming 20ms per frame. Target: 10ms.

## Changes

### Tick Throttling
- **DefaultCharacter**: Throttled `UpdateInteractHighlight()` and detection progress updates from 60Hz → 10Hz (100ms intervals)
- **GhostCharacterActor**: Throttled mesh/material updates from 60Hz → 20Hz (50ms intervals); added conditionals to skip redundant `SetLeaderPoseComponent()` calls; kept position interpolation at 60Hz
- **HackComponent/SearchComponent**: Set `PrimaryComponentTick.TickInterval = 0.05f` (60Hz → 20Hz)

### Tick Elimination  
- **CodeGenerator**: Replaced `Tick()` with `FTimerHandle` at 0.5s intervals for code expiry checks
- **DefaultPlayerController, CivilianCharacter, GuardCharacter**: Set `bCanEverTick = false` (no Tick implementations)

## Implementation Example

```cpp
void ADefaultCharacter::Tick(float DeltaTime)
{
    Super::Tick(DeltaTime);

    const float CurrentTime = GetWorld()->GetTimeSeconds();

    // Throttle from 60Hz to 10Hz
    if (IsLocallyControlled())
    {
        if (CurrentTime - LastInteractHighlightUpdateTime >= InteractHighlightUpdateInterval)
        {
            UpdateInteractHighlight();
            LastInteractHighlightUpdateTime = CurrentTime;
        }
    }

    // Similar throttling for detection updates...
}
```

## Performance Impact

- DefaultCharacter: 83% reduction in per-frame line traces and detection checks
- GhostCharacterActor: 67% reduction in expensive mesh operations  
- CodeGenerator: 97% reduction (60 calls/s → 2 calls/s)
- Components: 67% reduction during ability execution

Throttle intervals chosen to remain imperceptible: 100ms << 250ms human reaction time, 50ms < 42ms cinematic frame time.

